SUMMARY:Pressed Flower Candle Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a morning of hands-on pressed flower candle making!\nDiscover the simple\, satisfying craft of flower pressing and transform a plain pillar candle into a one-of-a-kind keepsake. Using warm palette knives to gently melt pressed flowers directly into the wax\, you’ll learn a technique that’s part botanical art\, part patience. Choose from a variety of pressed flowers to design your own arrangement. Beginners welcome.\n \nEach attendee will receive one 6″ white pillar candle\, a full selection of pressed flowers to choose from\, and step-by-step guidance on using heated palette knives safely to melt your design into the wax.\n \nSaturday\, November 28\, 10 to 11:30 a.m.\nPublic $65\, TBG Members $60 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Epiphanie Belanger\nEpiphanie Belanger is the founder of HobbyHub\, a community-driven platform designed to help people try new hobbies in a relaxed environment. What started as a personal curiosity for creative pursuits quickly turned into a mission to make hobbies more accessible\, social\, and fun for beginners.\n \nThrough curated workshops and experiences\, Epiphanie brings people together to explore hands-on creative skills in a welcoming\, low-pressure environment. Epiphanie is passionate about helping people rediscover play\, slow down\, and connect (both with their creativity and with others) one hobby at a time.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\n \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/pressed-flower-candle-workshop/
