SUMMARY:Seasonal Wreath Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an early start to the festive season by making a wonderful fresh aromatic evergreen wreath for your front door!\nDuring the workshop\, you’ll learn techniques of wreath making\, including selecting the perfect greenery\, arranging the materials\, and adding unique decor.\n \nBeginners welcome. Materials provided.\n \nOptional items to bring:\n \n\nGardening gloves\nItems to decorate your wreath (We will have ribbon and other festive items available\, but you are welcome to bring other decor you would like to decorate your wreath with.)\nGardening shears or secateurs\nWire cutters\n\nSaturday\, November 28\, 1 to 2:30 p.m.\nPublic $75\, Members $70 (plus applicable taxes and fees)\n \nAbout Lil Taggart\n \nLil Taggart is an experienced and creative designer and instructor in floral arts. She is also an accredited floral design judge and has competed on an international level as well as domestically. She served on the board of Canada Blooms\, co-chairs the staging for the Toronto Flower Show\, is past president of the Georgetown Horticultural Society\, and is a member of The Garden Club of Toronto.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\n \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/seasonal-wreath-workshop-2/
