SUMMARY:Paper Quilling: Holiday Gnome Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a fun-filled workshop on paper quilling and learn how to make amazing art with paper strips!\nIn the spirit of the holidays\, join us for a creative and relaxing experience surrounded by the beauty of Toronto Botanical Garden! In this hands-on workshop\, you’ll learn the art of paper quilling and create a stunning artwork from paper strips.\n \nPerfect for beginners and craft lovers alike\, this session will guide you step by step through rolling\, shaping\, and assembling paper strips into a masterpiece on a 5″x7″ canvas. Whether you’re coming with friends\, family\, or enjoying some creative “me time\,” you’ll leave with a beautiful handmade piece and a new skill to cherish\n \nAll materials provided. Suitable for adults and children ages 10 and above.\n \nSaturday\, December 5\, 2 to 4 p.m.\nPublic $50\, TBG Members $45 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Deepa Krishnan\nDeepa Krishnan is a self-taught artist specializing in the art of paper quilling\, which involves manipulating narrow strips of paper to create exquisite designs. She discovered this art form when she was looking for a creative outlet from her engineering job. She was amazed by the possibilities and beauty of paper quilling\, that she decided to pursue it as a full-time career. Since then\, she has been passionately mastering this technique and has created many artworks drawing inspiration from nature\, music and travel. She cuts the paper strips in different widths to add depth and dimension to her creations. She loves to play with the colours and experiment with the quilling techniques to create her own distinctive style. Deepa believes that anyone can learn this art form\, regardless of their age or skill level and she hosts many workshops to spread the joy of quilling. She enjoys seeing her students discover their own creativity and style in paper quilling.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/paper-quilling-holiday-gnome-workshop/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Art
