SUMMARY:Floral Design Program: Classic Design Fundamentals 2
DESCRIPTION:In this follow-up to Classic Design Fundamentals 1\, you will enrich your understanding of traditional design.\nEnrich your understanding of traditional design\, a style which is used in contemporary settings with sophistication. You will gain deeper knowledge of both plant material and design. You will learn colour theory: the importance of colour and how to create different colour harmonies. You will explore the concept and importance of asymmetry in a design and how this can be used to great effect. Discover a new design style each week: a hand-tied bouquet\, a vertical line design\, a Hogarth Curve and an asymmetrical mass design.\n \nCourse fees do not include flowers or supplies. Students are encouraged to find a local flower shop or grocery store to purchase their flowers. A materials list will be emailed prior to the start of each class.\n \nLearn more about our Certificate in Floral Design\n \nPrerequisites: Classic Design Fundamentals 1.\n \nThursday\, January 7\, 14\, 27 and 28\, 6 to 9 p.m.\nPublic $245\, Members $195 (plus applicable taxes and fees)\n \nAbout Margaret Betts\nMarg Betts is a floral design judge with accreditation to judge and instruct the craft. Her passions are gardening\, plants and her love for creating floral artistry. She is a recent past President of the Garden Club of Toronto and has also been the Chair of the Toronto Flower Show at Canada Blooms.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program\, please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/floral-design-program-classic-design-fundamentals-2-13/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
